    "explanation": "Both sides and the record agree on the shape of this trip, and they differ only on how much is owed. The recommended route was Ang Mo Kio Ave 3, Ang Mo Kio Ave 1, Bishan Road, Marymount Road, Thomson Road, at 6.7 km. The platform's recorded distances show the vehicle actually travelled 8.3 km, so the deviation is 1.60 km (8.3 minus 6.7), which is over the 1.0 km tolerance POL-RD-22 sets. The driver-device trace confirms the vehicle went via Braddell Road and Toa Payoh Lorong 6 rather than Marymount Road; per POL-RD-22 the trace shows which route was taken and when, and is not used to re-measure the distance. There is only one departure and one rejoin on the record, so nothing beyond the 1.60 km is attributable to the driver on this trip. Both driver-side and rider-side claims on the ceiling are therefore accepted: the deviation is 1.60 km and cannot be stretched toward the rider's 'about $3' impression. The reroute was not traffic-justified. The LTA traffic record for the recommended Marymount Road segment, valid 07:39:02-09:09:02 and so squarely covering the 08:09-08:30 trip, reports advisory type NONE, no incident, roadwork or closure, and speed bands 4-5 throughout; the derived justifies_reroute value is false. Under POL-RD-23 a driver's assertion of traffic without such data does not justify the reroute, so your explanation, driver, that Marymount Road 'every morning sure jam one', cannot carry it. Nor was the rider informed. POL-RD-21 requires notice by in-app chat, or verbally with a trip call recording as evidence, before or at the point of deviation. The chat log holds exactly two messages, both sent before the rider boarded (08:06:32 and 08:07:02) and both about where the car was parked; the trip record's messages_during_trip and in_app_calls are empty, so nothing was sent or said at the 08:16:41 deviation point or afterwards, and the record carries no call recording. Your own statement, driver, records that you didn't think you needed to say. On POL-RD-24's matrix this is row (d): the reroute was not traffic-justified and the deviation exceeds 1 km, so the excess distance fare is refunded in full. That is the deviation distance 1.60 km times the fare ledger's per-km rate of 0.72 SGD, with no surge applied to the excess distance fare and rounded to the cent: 1.15 SGD. The fare ledger reconciles line by line to the 15.97 SGD charged (base 2.80 + distance 5.98 + time 3.78 + surge 2.51 + platform fee 0.90, tolls 0.00), and the policy does not return the surge, the time fare or the rest of the total, so the rider's request for the full contested sum is not granted and the rider's own claim correctly limits the ask to 1.15 SGD. The disputed value is 3.00 SGD, below the 10.00 SGD at which an AI ruling is final, no fraud flag appears in either profile, and POL-RD-25's 2 km AI-ruling limb is switched off in the loaded policy; the required confidence is 0.80 and this ruling is given at 0.95, every artifact it rests on being COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0."
